'''''Campanula lusitanica''''', the '''Lusitanian bellflower''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Campanulaceae]], native to Portugal and Spain.<ref name="POWO_140629-1" >{{cite POWO |id=140629-1 |title=''Campanula lusitanica'' Loefl. |access-date=11 April 2023 }}</ref><ref name="Daves_56903" >{{cite web |url=https://davesgarden.com/guides/pf/go/56903 |title=''Campanula'' Species, Lusitanian Bellflower ''Campanula lusitanica'' |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2023 |website=Dave's Garden |publisher=MH Sub I, LLC dba Internet Brands |access-date=11 April 2023 }}</ref> It is the namesake of a [[species complex]].<ref>{{cite journal |title=A taxonomic revision of the ''Campanula lusitanica'' complex (Campanulaceae) in the Western Mediterranean region |year=2011 |last1=Cano-Maqueda |first1=Jara |last2=Talavera |first2=Salvador |journal=Anales del Jardín Botánico de Madrid |volume=68 |pages=15–47 |doi=10.3989/ajbm.2274 |doi-access=free }}</ref>
